  "qualifications": [
    "All four constructions, drawing options, toggles, numeric coefficient/default prompts and successful preference retention",
    "Captured CPlanes, rotated/spatial axes, negative origins, signed extents, focus-only and empty results",
    "Exact NURBS controls, weights, degree, full knots, domain, object order, selection, finite lengths and actual undo/redo",
    "Construction changes at the focus getter: three completed live input traces with native Cancel, no timeout, no injected Cancel",
    "Projected conic weights across CPlane tilts, coefficient families and spatial opening axes",
    "Analytic denominator-pole fractions, common weight gauges, reparameterization, fast length rejection and viewport gaps at non-dyadic poles",
    "Two fresh Conic commands preserve physical hover and edge-pick acknowledgements after sharing the managed input driver"
  ],
  "metric_policy": "For a clamped quadratic with weights [1,w,1], w<=-1 proves a denominator pole. Rhino GetLength returns zero for the measured projective cases; the probe tags this SDK failure result with length_query_failed=true. The Rust geometry API returns ZeroWeightAtParameter. These values are not interpreted as zero finite arc lengths. Controls and weights remain unnormalized.",
